.TH GET 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
get \- retrieve a version of an SCCS file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B get
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR SID ]
.I s.file
.RI [ s.file ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B get
retrieves the text of the delta named by
.B \-r
(or, if
.B \-r
is not given, the file's own sole delta) from each
.I s.file
operand.
.PP
This implementation only ever reads a single-delta SCCS file: one
created by
.BR admin (1)
and never modified since, whose one delta always has the SCCS ID
(SID)
.BR 1.1 .
There is no counterpart to
.BR delta (1)
in this project to have ever committed a second delta, so a
.I s.file
with more than one delta is not something this implementation can
produce or has ever been tested against.
.PP
Without
.BR \-p ,
the retrieved text is written to a new file (the "g-file") named by
dropping the \(dqs.\(dq prefix from
.IR s.file 's
own basename, in the same directory, and a two-line status message
.RI ( SID ,
then the line count) is written to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p
Write the retrieved text to standard output instead of creating a
g-file. The two-line status message that would otherwise go to
standard output is written to standard error instead, so \(dqget \-p
s.file\(dq can be piped without also piping the status message.
.TP
.BI \-r " SID"
Retrieve the delta named
.IR SID .
Since every
.I s.file
this implementation can read has exactly one delta,
.I SID
must name that file's own delta (always
.BR 1.1 )
or this is a diagnosed error. May also be written attached, as
.BI \-r SID
with no intervening space.
.PP
Every other
.B get
option (including
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-b ,
.BR \-c ,
.BR \-e ,
.BR \-g ,
.BR \-i ,
.BR \-k ,
.BR \-l ,
.BR \-L ,
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-n ,
.BR \-s ,
and
.BR \-x ,
all of which a real
.B get
uses to select among or edit a multi-delta history) is refused with a
diagnostic; none of them is implemented. Reading a \(dq\-\(dq operand
as a list of filenames on standard input is likewise not implemented.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I s.file
The pathname of an SCCS file to retrieve from. Its basename must begin
with the literal two characters \(dqs.\(dq.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every
.I s.file
operand was retrieved successfully.
.TP
.B >0
An operand was skipped (missing, not a valid SCCS file, wrong
basename, or the requested SID did not match the file's own delta);
processing continues with any remaining operands. Also returned for a
usage error (no operand given, or an unimplemented option used).
.SH EXAMPLES
Retrieve the checked-in text of
.B s.hello.c
straight to standard output:
.nf
get \-p s.hello.c
.fi
.PP
Retrieve it into a g-file named
.B hello.c
instead:
.nf
get s.hello.c
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR admin (1)
